vtun for DEBIAN
----------------------

the installed /etc/vtund.conf file is empty except for explanatory comments.

I split up the original example file into two files: one for a server
configuration and one for a client configuration.  These examples are
located in /usr/doc/vtun

By default, vtund doesn't start at all, you need to edit /etc/vtund.conf
and set it up for your requirements.  See the docs and examples for
details.

you also need to edit /etc/vtund-start.conf and define whether vtund is
being run as a client or as a server.  See the man page.

you'll also need to create proper device nodes for the tun
devices. 2.2 kernels there is now a tun-source package in debian.
2.4 kernels, the tun/tap driver is integrated. You'll need to create
the device yourself.

mknod /dev/misc/net/tun c 10 200

Greg Olszewski <noop@debian.org>
